{"name":"Twin Cities","hex":"#a4c7c8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Twin Cities","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The metropolitan area of Minneapolis and Saint Paul, Minnesota."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Twin_Cities"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twin cities","blocks":[{"text":"Twin cities are a special case of two neighboring cities or urban centers that grow into a single conurbation, or narrowly separated urban areas, over time. Twin cities are generally comparable in status and size, though not necessarily equal. Although there are no formal criteria, a city and a substantially smaller suburb would not typically qualify, even if they were once separate. Tri-cities and quad cities are similar groups of three or four municipalities, respectively."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg/330px-Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twin_cities","wikidata":"Q244793"},{"title":"Minneapolis–Saint Paul","blocks":[{"text":"Minneapolis–Saint Paul is a major metropolitan area built around the confluence of the Mississippi, Minnesota, and St. Croix rivers in east central Minnesota. The area is commonly known as the Twin Cities after its two largest cities, Minneapolis, the state's most populous city, and its neighbor to the east, Saint Paul, the capital. Minnesotans often refer to the two together as \"the Cities.\" It is the third-largest metropolitan area in the Midwest and the 16th-largest metropolitan statistical area in the U.S."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg/330px-Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minneapolis%E2%80%93Saint_Paul","wikidata":"Q1480013"},{"title":"Twin","blocks":[{"text":"Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. Twins can be either monozygotic ('identical'), meaning that they develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic, meaning that each twin develops from a separate egg and each egg is fertilized by its own sperm cell. Since identical twins develop from one zygote, they will share the same chromosomal sex, while fraternal twins may or may not. In very rare cases, fraternal or (semi-) identical twins can have the same mother and different fathers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Mauch_Twins.jpg/330px-Mauch_Twins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twin","wikidata":"Q159979"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg/500px-Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg/1280px-Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg/500px-Cedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"High-rise buildings in Minneapolis's Cedar-Riverside neighborhood, with the Downtown Saint Paul skyline visible in the background ten miles away. Minneapolis' city limits border those of Saint Paul, the capital of Minnesota. This gave birth to the nickname of the region, the \"Twin Cities\" metropolitan area.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACedar-Riverside_and_Saint_Paul_skyline_seen_from_the_Foshay_Tower_observation_deck%2C_May_2018.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG/500px-View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG/1280px-View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG/500px-View_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view of the town of Tornio (Finland), which forms a twin city with Haparanda (Sweden)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AView_from_Suensaari_water_tower_Tornio_20150806_04.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg/500px-Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg/1280px-Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg/500px-Obelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-border example of twin cities: Plaza Internacional of the Frontera de la Paz. On the left, Santana do Livramento (Brazil); on the right, Rivera (Uruguay).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AObelisco_-_Plaza_Internacional_-_Frontera_de_la_Paz_-_Livramento_-_Rivera.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg/500px-Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg/1280px-Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg/500px-Minneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinneapolis_Skyline_looking_south.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Saint_Paul_skyline%2C_West_Side_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Saint_Paul_skyline%2C_West_Side_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Saint_Paul_skyline%2C_West_Side_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Saint_Paul_skyline%2C_West_Side_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaint_Paul_skyline%2C_West_Side_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg/500px-Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg/1280px-Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg/500px-Stillwater-2004-01-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"St. Croix River in Stillwater","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStillwater-2004-01-02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Stpaul001.jpg/500px-Stpaul001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Stpaul001.jpg/500px-Stpaul001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"St. Paul with barges on the Mississippi River, the Capitol dome, and Minneapolis's skyline in the far background (right of St. Paul). In the lower right is a typical 19th century home in Indian Mounds Park.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStpaul001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg/500px-Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg/1280px-Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg/500px-Ford_lock_and_dam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lock and Dam No. 1 on the Mississippi River upstream from the Minnesota River","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFord_lock_and_dam.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}